# Completion review: approved auto-quality-band OpenSpec packages

Date: 2026-10-03
Scope: activation and publication preparation for the three approved packages
in `openspec/changes/`, plus repository-level deferred work in
`openspec/TODO.md`.

## Recorded decisions

- Band channels default to `thrifty` only while `OMNIROUTE_AUTO_BANDS` is on.
  With the flag off, omitted tier stays unset for upstream default handling;
  explicit tiers retain upstream behavior.
- Unrated models pass only `low`; they receive no synthetic fitness score and
  remain outside mid/high calibration populations.
- The old `agt` role maps to `general + tools`.
- Enabled band `thrifty` channels order eligible rungs `free → keyless →
  subscription → cheap → premium`. Plain upstream `auto:thrifty` ordering is
  unchanged. The flag-off path bypasses band order, quality/capability filters,
  reserve, and account narrowing.
- Reserve removes reserved account IDs before band rung ordering and dispatch;
  it retains candidates with at least one account left and drops candidates
  whose allowed IDs are all reserved.
- Explicit `:free` preserves upstream provider/model classification, including
  eligible keyless OpenCode models. It is not a per-connection zero-spend
  guarantee.
- The shared upstream integration points are `suffixComposition.ts` and
  `virtualFactory.ts`; runtime implementation remains deferred.

## Validation

- Code Simplifier skill review applied to the docs-only change: clarified
  degraded-category pseudocode without changing behavior or approved decisions.
- Strict OpenSpec validation passed directly in the repository for all three
  packages using the standard `openspec/changes/<id>` layout:
  `add-auto-band-seam`, `add-auto-quality-band-filter`, and
  `add-auto-band-demand-reserve` (after the final edits).
- Production/database, calibration coverage, factory-hook and reserve shadow
  checks are listed in `openspec/TODO.md` and remain unrun.

## Scope status

No runtime code was changed. Packages are active in `openspec/changes/` and
their approved index is `openspec/README.md`. Documentation commit
was created; remote push is pending. No `completion.review` existed in this
repository before this review record was created.
